+When a review command returns results to the controller, the patch-agent chat receives the review
+summary and a `work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no` confirmation line. A `yes` reply is recorded
+in the patch-agent transcript and closes the feature chat. A `no` reply records the reopened state
+without sending that confirmation text to the agent backend. Any other follow-up text reopens the
+feature chat and is sent to the patch agent as the next user message.
+
 The command transcript is also the conversation history for the persistent `command-agent`. That
 system agent interprets chat sent to the Work Leaf command surface. It recognizes literal command
 lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quitting, and launching
@@ -288,6 +294,11 @@ When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the
 `/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the same selected-agent chat
 path.
 
+The terminal cache treats the feature completion prompt, closed marker, and reopened marker as
+ordered state markers rather than duplicate transcript lines. A closed feature chat is hidden from
+the left pane and does not display a ready marker. A reopened feature chat becomes visible again and
+uses the normal ready-state calculation when it is not loading.
+
 The terminal app maps a session to a left-pane `READY` marker when the controller exposes no loading
 state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
